git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/dev/trunk@1140859 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by an incorrect handling of document offsets when transitioning to the use of `AtomicReaderContext`. Specifically, the original implementation used an intermediary `offset` variable that likely did not correctly reflect the document base, leading to incorrect document value retrieval during search operations.

Here is the patch:

   @Override
   public DocValues getValues(Map context, AtomicReaderContext readerContext) throws IOException {
-    int offset = 0;
+    final int off = readerContext.docBase;
     ReaderContext topLevelContext = ReaderUtil.getTopLevelContext(readerContext);
-    final int off = offset;

     final float[] arr = getCachedFloats(topLevelContext.reader);
     return new FloatDocValues(this) {
       @Override
       public float floatVal(int doc) {
         return arr[doc + off];
       }

       @Override
       public Object objectVal(int doc) {
         return floatVal(doc);   // TODO: keep track of missing values
       }
     };
   }



